-> [[docs:guide-user:installation:generic.flashing|Install OpenWrt (generic explanation)]]


A **TTL USB serial adapter** and disassembly is required to gain access to the SamKnows-customized OpenWrt distribution, as telnet and SSH are not accessible on the SamKnows stock firmware, even in the failsafe environment.

  - [[#opening_the_case|Open the case]]
  - Use your favorite software to connect to the [[#serial|serial port]] at 57600 8N1
  - Power the router up and as soon as the bootcount message appears (after about 3 seconds), power down.
  - Repeat this process many times, until you get bootdelay that allows to choose a u-boot option.
  - Now that you can select the TFTP option, use Debricking procedure below.
===== Debricking =====

You will need access to the [[#serial|serial port]] to debrick if you flash an image that does not boot. The SamKnows Whitebox 8's U-Boot is able to flash OpenWrt images loaded from TFTP.

  - Get [[#serial|serial access]]
  - Upon power up, type "2" to re-flash via TFTP
  - Type "Y" to confirm overwrite of existing firmware
  - Follow the prompts to set IP addresses
  - The router will flash the firmware and automatically reboot when complete

===== Failsafe mode =====

  - WIP firmware that has correctly defined WPS GPIO for failsafe
  - Stock SamKnows firmware goes into failsafe mode with WPS button, but dropbear is password protected on port 2222

